## Summary

### 1. `polkagent-harness-opencode` — ACP-pattern harness for OpenCode

**`crates/polkagent-harness-opencode/Cargo.toml`** — workspace crate depending on `polkagent-harness-trait` and `polkagent-harness-acp`

**`crates/polkagent-harness-opencode/src/lib.rs`** — follows the exact same pattern as cursor/goose/kiro:
- `OpenCodeTransport` enum (ACP variant)
- `OpenCodeHarnessConfig` + builder
- `OpenCodeConfigurator` implementing `AcpConfigurator` trait (harness ID `"opencode"`, binary `opencode acp`, 200K context, claude-sonnet-4-6 model)
- `OpenCodeHarness` type alias for `AcpHarness<OpenCodeConfigurator>`
- 15 tests covering configurator, config, serde, builder, binary resolution

### 2. `polkagent-harness-bridge` — generic HTTP/WebSocket bridge harness

**`crates/polkagent-harness-bridge/Cargo.toml`** — workspace crate depending on `polkagent-harness-trait` and `reqwest`

**`crates/polkagent-harness-bridge/src/lib.rs`** — directly implements the `Harness` trait (no ACP):
- `BridgeTransport` enum (`HttpPost`, `WebSocket`)
- `BridgeConfig` with `endpoint`, `auth_token`, `timeout`, `transport` fields + builder
- `BridgeHarness` implementing all `Harness` trait methods over HTTP POST using `reqwest`
- Proper session tracking, auth header injection, health endpoint
- 14 tests covering config, capabilities, serde, session error handling

### 3. Supporting changes

- **`crates/polkagent-harness-acp/src/lib.rs`** — added `AcpConfig::opencode()` constructor
- **`Cargo.toml`** — added both crates to workspace members

